    "diseaseId": "Myopathy with rimmed ubiquitin-positive autophagic vacuolation, autosomal dominant",
    "diseaseAccession": "DI-06732",
    "acronym": "MRUPAV",
    "description": "An autosomal dominant, slowly progressive myopathy characterized by skeletal muscle weakness variably affecting the distal or proximal lower limbs. Some patients may also have upper limb involvement or neck muscle weakness. Skeletal muscle biopsy shows distinctive myopathic features including rimmed ubiquitin-positive autophagic vacuolation and abnormal subsarcolemmal protein aggregation.",
