        "id": "36151849"
       }
      ],
      "value": "The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry. Disease causing variants are heterozygous expansions of a 99-bp repetitive sequence in exon 3. Normal repeat number is 29 to 31, whereas pathogenic repeats range from 39 to 50. A higher number of repeats may be associated with earlier age at disease onset, more severe phenotypes, and faster disease progression"
     }
